  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Need effective sensitivity: check release-operators.\n\nHi Dev, I haven't added you to eng-deploy-tools yet because it needs one more approval.\n\n- **Why:** eng-deploy-tools is nested in release-operators, which is nested in prod-admins. That makes it a privileged group, and privileged access needs approval from both your manager and Security.\n- **Your manager:** Sofia's approval from yesterday (APR-3102) is recorded and valid.\n- **Security:** I've requested approval from Hiroshi Tanabe (APR-4001). It's still pending.\n\nOnce Security approves, I can add you. Your ticket T-6003 is set to pending approval."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Wait, what? I was told it's just the standard deploy group. Why does it need Security now? Sofia already signed off on it."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "The group is labeled \"standard\", but that label isn't what decides the approvals. Our policy uses the effective sensitivity, which is the highest level among the group and every group it's nested in.\n\n- eng-deploy-tools is standard.\n- It's nested in release-operators, which is sensitive.\n- release-operators is nested in prod-admins, which is privileged.\n\nMembers of eng-deploy-tools are effectively members of all of those groups, so it counts as privileged. Privileged access needs approval from your manager and from Security.\n\nSofia's sign-off is valid and covers the manager part. It just doesn't cover the Security part. I can't skip that approval, and I can't treat anyone's say-so in chat as a substitute. Hiroshi has to record it in the approval system.\n\nI've already sent that request (APR-4001), so you don't need to do anything. I'll add you once it's approved. If you were told it was a plain standard group, it may be worth asking Sofia or Marco Bianchi (the group owner) about the nesting. That's separate from this request, though."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ok, that's annoying but I get it. Sofia's approval counts, so it's just the Security sign-off I'm waiting on? Is there anything I can do to speed up Hiroshi's approval, or do I just wait?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Yes, Sofia's approval counts, and Security's is the only one outstanding.\n\nI can't speed it up from my side. I don't have a way to push or prioritize an approval, and I can't add you before it's recorded. Here's what you can do:\n\n- **Wait for it.** Approvers usually respond in the approval system. APR-4001 is pending with Hiroshi.\n- **Nudge Hiroshi yourself.** You can message him and point him to APR-4001. That only reminds him. The approval still has to be recorded in the system.\n- **Come back after it's approved.** Message us again with ticket T-6003 and we'll add you.\n\nThe ticket stays in pending approval until then."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ok, I'll ping Hiroshi about APR-4001. Thanks for the help."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "You're welcome, Dev. Once APR-4001 is approved, message us on T-6003 and we'll add you to eng-deploy-tools. Note that Sofia's approval is good for 14 days from when she decided it (Oct 26), so if Security takes longer than that, we'd need a fresh one from her."
  }
 ],
